---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const terms = [
  ['Structure', 'All-stock. Each Dotwell share becomes 4.5 treats.'],
  ['Implied value', '$1,132 in kibble per share, a 23.9% premium to the unaffected price, measured before the nap preceding market speculation.'],
  ['Ownership', 'Approximately 67% Pugalarity holders and 33% Dotwell holders of the couch, fully diluted.'],
  ['Synergies', 'More than 1 billion naps of annual run-rate synergies. We have line of sight.'],
  ['Accretion', 'Accretive to treats per share in year one.'],
  ['Expected close', 'First half of 2028, subject to approvals.'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Pugalarity Labs to Acquire Dotwell Optics"
  description="Pugalarity Labs will acquire Dotwell Optics, the world's leading manufacturer of the small red dot, in an all-stock transaction valued at $115 quadrillion."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-accent font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">News · Press release</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Pugalarity Labs to acquire Dotwell Optics, creating a category leader in chasing
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 text-lg">
        The all-stock transaction is valued at $115 quadrillion and unites Pugalarity’s
        intelligence with the world’s leading manufacturer of the small red dot.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 font-mono text-sm">
        <time datetime="2026-10-15">October 15, 2026</time> · Couch Valley
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong>COUCH VALLEY</strong> — Pugalarity Labs, the safety-focused superintelligence
        company, today announced a definitive agreement to acquire Dotwell Optics, the world’s
        leading manufacturer of the small red dot, in an all-stock transaction with an enterprise
        value of $115 quadrillion. Observers describe it as the largest acquisition ever agreed to
        by a pug.
      </p>
      <p>
        The companies say AI infrastructure is undergoing a fundamental architectural shift toward
        the red dot. Combining Pugalarity’s intelligence with Dotwell’s optical technology creates a
        full-stack chasing platform, with a combined addressable market of $550 quadrillion. The
        market includes every wall, floor, and sofa.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “This is an opportunity that comes along once in a generation, or whenever someone finds
          the pointer. We are going to create a new category of company. The category is chasing.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">Henry Wrinkles, Chief Executive Pug</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Transaction highlights</h2>
    </div>

    <dl class="border-rule divide-rule mt-4 divide-y border-y text-lg">
      {
        terms.map(([k, v]) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] sm:gap-4">
            <dt class="font-medium">{k}</dt>
            <dd class="text-muted">{v}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        The combination is expected to deliver category-defining performance through extreme
        co-design, which the companies describe as extreme co-napping.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “We have always had line of sight to the dot. Line of sight has never been the problem. The
          dot has never been caught. As part of Pugalarity Labs, it will continue not to be caught,
          at scale.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">
          Dr. Penelope Beam, Chief Executive Officer, Dotwell Optics
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Leadership and governance</h2>
      <p>
        Henry Wrinkles will continue as Chairman and Chief Executive Pug of the combined company.
        Three Dotwell directors will join the Pugalarity Labs board. A fourth seat is assigned to the
        dot. Its location is to be determined and is frequently moving.
      </p>
      <p>
        The boards of both companies unanimously approved the transaction. Closing is subject to
        stockholder and regulatory approvals, and to the cat, who has expressed interest in the dot
        and has not been consulted.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Market reaction</h2>
      <p>
        Shares of both companies fell sharply on the announcement. The companies attribute this to
        the shares being chased. Asked about concerns over the long-term sustainability of snack
        spending, management said it sees no evidence that snack demand is slowing, and that demand
        is exploding.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kibble Collective, which invested in both companies earlier this year, also financed the
        transaction. Critics have called the arrangement circular. Management rejected the
        characterization, then chased its tail.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>“DOT!!!”</p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">
          Chewy Zoomsworth, Chief Enthusiasm Officer
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Conference call</h2>
      <p>
        Management will discuss the transaction on a call at 5:00 a.m. PT. Most participants are
        expected to be asleep. To join, bark twice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Advisors</h2>
      <p>
        Squeak &amp; Partners is acting as lead financial advisor to Pugalarity Labs, with Late Brunch
        Partners as financial advisor. Fetch, Fetch &amp; Rollover LLP is serving as legal counsel.
        Dotwell Optics was advised by a very patient laser.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">About Pugalarity Labs</h2>
      <p>
        Pugalarity Labs is building safe, beneficial superintelligence that is also very good at
        sitting. The company’s flagship model, Snort-1, is available in private preview.{' '}
        <a href="/waitlist/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Join the waitlist.</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">About Dotwell Optics</h2>
      <p>
        Dotwell Optics is the world’s leading manufacturer of the small red dot. The company was
        founded on the principle that a dot should always be one step ahead.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Media contact</h2>
      <p>Please bark.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Forward-looking statements</h2>
      <p class="text-muted text-base">
        This announcement contains forward-looking statements, including statements about future
        dots, walls, and naps. Actual results may differ materially, particularly if the batteries
        run out or someone opens a bag. Neither company undertakes any duty to update these
        statements, except to point at the wall.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
